<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1145 0 R
/E (The study utilizes Federated Learning \(FL\) to train machine learning models on decentralized data generated by vehicles and infrastructure in Intelligent Transportation Systems \(ITS\). FL enables local training on edge devices while aggregating model updates centrally, preserving data privacy and reducing communication overhead.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
570 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1146 0 R
/E (FL enhances privacy as raw data never leaves local devices, addressing data sharing and confidentiality concerns. It improves real-time processing by distributing computation across edge devices, reducing latency. FL also enables collaboration among multiple organizations without exposing sensitive data, fostering scalable and efficient ITS solutions.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
571 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1147 0 R
/E (Challenges in FL include high communication costs due to frequent model updates and heterogeneity in device capabilities causing slow or imbalanced training. Security risks exist from malicious participants potentially poisoning the aggregated model. Additionally, protecting against inference attacks and ensuring regulatory compliance remain complex issues.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
