582 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1150 0 R
/E (The paper proposes an Adaptive Segmentation Enhanced Asynchronous Federated Learning \(AS-AFL\) model for ITS, which groups vehicles with similar network and device characteristics using a meta-learning-based segmentation. Within groups, synchronous federated learning updates models via peer-to-peer exchanges, while across groups asynchronous updates enable scalable, reliable learning without a central server.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
583 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1151 0 R
/E (The paper proposes an Adaptive Segmentation Enhanced Asynchronous Federated Learning \(AS-AFL\) model for ITS, which groups vehicles with similar network and device characteristics using a meta-learning-based segmentation. Within groups, synchronous federated learning updates models via peer-to-peer exchanges, while across groups asynchronous updates enable scalable, reliable learning without a central server.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
584 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1152 0 R
/E (Challenges include the complexity of dynamically segmenting clients based on varied attributes and ensuring accurate group formation. The approach requires efficient peer-to-peer communication protocols and may face scalability issues in extremely large networks. Also, asynchronous updates might introduce inconsistencies affecting model convergence.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [32]
>>
endobj
