596 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1163 0 R
/E (The approach combines edge, fog, and cloud layers to manage IoT data processing efficiently. Edge devices perform local data preprocessing and lightweight analytics to reduce latency. Fog nodes act as intermediaries, handling more complex processing closer to data sources, while the cloud provides large-scale storage and heavy computational power for deep analytics.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
597 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1164 0 R
/E (This layered architecture balances latency reduction, bandwidth savings, and powerful analytics. It enables context-aware decision-making near the source of data and offloads intensive tasks to the cloud, achieving scalability. Containerization and orchestration techniques allow flexible deployment and dynamic resource allocation, improving system resilience and adaptability.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
598 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1165 0 R
/E (Challenges include complex task allocation and scheduling across heterogeneous networks and devices, managing security and privacy across distributed nodes, and handling variable network conditions. Ensuring seamless coordination between layers and mitigating data redundancy or communication bottlenecks add to design complexity.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
